{
 "rule": "errors.try-catch-outside-boundaries",
 "guide": "Follows the allowed list in canopy CLAUDE.md literally, with no additions: try/catch is allowed only for PTY or process cleanup (kill, taskkill, tmux kill-session), HTTP request parsing, JSON.parse on untrusted input, contextBridge initialization, and file cleanup (rm/unlink of files the code created, or cleanup in finally); try/finally without catch is not a try/catch. Everything else in main-process code is a violation, including new URL, YAML parsing, closing views or servers, chmod, unsubscribe, crash reporter code, IPC handlers, and catch blocks that convert to err() instead of using fromExternalCall(). A team that wants any of these allowed should add it to CLAUDE.md first; the labels and the rule then follow.",
 "labeled_by": "Claude, 2026-09-23, from reading each hunk",
